**Goal Model – Multi‑Robot Resource Delivery Mission**

| **Name** | **Text** | **Runtime** | **Goal Type** | **Target Condition / Enquired Info** | **Relation** | **Justification** |
|----------|----------|-------------|---------------|-------------------------------------|--------------|-------------------|
| **G1: Complete Resource Delivery Mission** | Achieve the delivery of all requested resources to the specified destination. | `;` | Achieve | All requested resources delivered to destination. | AND | The mission is split into two mandatory phases – collection and delivery – that must be finished one after the other. |
| **G2: Collect Resources** | Perform the collection of resources from storage locations. | `FALLBACK((G3 AND G4 AND G5), G6)` | Perform | – | AND | Collection consists of navigation, request and wait. If the robot’s battery drops below 10 % the normal flow must be abandoned in favour of the battery‑low handling sub‑goal. |
| **G3: Navigate to Storage** | Navigate to the storage location where the resource is located. | `-` | Perform | – | AND | The robot must physically travel to the storage before any request can be sent. |
| **G4: Request Resource** | Send a request message to the storage for the specified resources. | `-` | Perform | – | AND | The robot must explicitly request the items before they can be retrieved. |
| **G5: Wait for Retrieval** | Wait until the storage retrieves the requested resources. | `-` | Perform | – | AND | The robot must pause until the resources are ready for pickup. |
| **G6: Battery Low in Collection Phase** | Handle low battery during collection by recharging and re‑assigning the mission. | `;` | Perform | – | AND | When the battery falls below 10 % the robot must recharge and hand the task over to another robot. |
| **G7: Deliver Resources** | Perform the delivery of collected resources to the destination. | `FALLBACK((G8 AND G9), G10)` | Perform | – | AND | Delivery requires navigation to the destination and the actual hand‑over. If the battery drops below 30 % the robot must return to a checkpoint and re‑assign. |
| **G8: Navigate to Destination** | Navigate to the destination location where resources must be delivered. | `-` | Perform | – | AND | The robot must travel to the delivery point before it can hand over the items. |
| **G9: Deliver Resources to Destination** | Deliver the collected resources to the destination location. | `-` | Perform | – | AND | The robot must physically deliver the items. |
| **G10: Return to Checkpoint and Re‑assign** | Return the resource to a checkpoint and re‑assign the remaining task to another robot. | `FALLBACK((G11 AND G12), G13)` | Perform | – | AND | If the battery is low during delivery the robot must first return to a checkpoint and then hand the task over. If the return fails an alert must be sent. |
| **G11: Return to Checkpoint** | Return the resource to a checkpoint location. | `-` | Perform | – | AND | The robot must bring the resource to a safe location before handing over. |
| **G12: Assign Mission to Another Robot** | Assign the remaining delivery task to another robot. | `-` | Perform | – | AND | The robot must re‑assign the task so that the mission can continue. |
| **G13: Alert Sector Manager** | Trigger an alert and send a report to the sector manager. | `-` | Perform | – | AND | If the robot cannot return to the checkpoint, an alert must be raised. |

